{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the morrow</b> — with the letters, gematria of למחר יום כפורים, with the words:" "<b>from the morning unto the evening</b> — and it does not say ועד. Hint: the time of a court is until six hours. Corresponding to the six times that are written in the portion: לשפוט, ושפטתי, ושפטו, and it is written הבקר עד הערב — heh, heh; the extra heh below says only מן בקר עד ערב, to say: whoever judges a true judgment to its truth, it is as though he became a partner to the Holy One, blessed be He, in the work of Creation, which was created with heh."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:31.022309421Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}